    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7649": {
      "title": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Director of Simulation and Clinical Lab Operations",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Director of Simulation and Clinical Lab Operations Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Director of Simulation and Clinical Lab Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra Hofstra University is nationally ranked and recognized as Long Island’s largest private university located in Hempstead, N.Y. When you work at Hofstra, you join a team of talented professionals committed to preparing students for the challenges of tomorrow, in an environment that cultivates learning through the free and open exchange of ideas for the betterment of humankind. The work we do at Hofstra supports the education and well-being of our students, and the workforce of the future. While working towards this mission, employees can take advantage of many enriching experiences on campus. Whether it’s a lunchtime lecture, a Division I NCAA athletics game, a musical concert, a theatre performance, or a visit to one of our two accredited museums, there is always something exciting to do at Hofstra. Enjoy the ease of going to the fitness center, taking a swim, or grabbing a bite to eat without having to leave our beautiful campus! Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Director of Simulation and Clinical Lab Operations Position Number 896653 Position Category Administration School/Division Hofstra Northwell School of Nursing and Physician Assistant Studies Department Office of the Dean, School of Nursing and Physician Assistant Studies Full-Time or Part-Time Full-Time Description Reporting to the Vice Dean, the Director of Simulation and Clinical Lab Operations will support the undergraduate and graduate nursing programs in the School of Nursing and Physician Assistant Studies. The Director of Simulation and Clinical Lab Operations manages instructional and administrative leadership in the simulation education space and functions within the Hofstra Northwell School of Nursing and Physician Assistant Studies under the supervision of the Office of the Dean. This is a year-round administrator position with responsibilities managing the schedule and curricular delivery in highly specialized advanced medical simulation and clinical laboratory spaces. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Ensures simulation and standardized patient (SP) experiences align with the Hofstra Northwell School of Nursing and Physician Assistant Studies ( SONPA ) mission, vision, strategic plan, institutional learning outcomes, and applicable state and national standards. Provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for all simulation, clinical skills, and standardized patient programs within the Science and Innovation Center. Oversees staffing, scheduling, daily operations, and budget planning for simulation and clinical skills activities across SONPA academic programs. Supervises the Clinical Simulation Educator, Standardized Patient Administrator, and other assigned personnel, providing leadership, mentorship, and performance oversight. Collaborates with the Nursing Department Chair, Assistant Chair for Undergraduate Nursing, Vice Dean, and faculty to coordinate priorities, scheduling, and operations of the Clinical Skills Laboratory, including open laboratory opportunities. Oversees the maintenance, inventory, procurement, and operational readiness of simulation equipment, clinical supplies, laboratory resources, and simulation spaces to ensure a safe and effective learning environment. Coordinates simulation program accreditation activities, including applications, renewals, reporting, program assessment, advisory committee support, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. Develops, facilitates, and evaluates simulation-based learning experiences, including simulation scenarios, standardized patient encounters, learner debriefing, and interprofessional education activities. Oversees all aspects of the Standardized Patient (SP) program, including recruitment, selection, onboarding, training, scheduling, event coordination, performance evaluation, and collaboration with faculty on case development and implementation. Administers the Education Management Solution ( EMS ) SimulationiQ platform, including scheduling simulation events, managing cases, checklists and assessment materials, coordinating video recording and archiving, generating reports, and troubleshooting hardware and software issues during simulation activities. Coordinates the maintenance, upgrades, and ongoing functionality of EMS SimulationiQ and other simulation technologies in collaboration with Hofstra Information Technology, EMS representatives, and other technology vendors; maintains current knowledge of emerging simulation technologies and best practices. Leads simulation-related projects and collaborates with Northwell Health’s Center for Learning and Innovation and other institutional partners to advance simulation education and innovation. Develops and supports admissions events, marketing initiatives, community outreach, continuing education programs, and other activities that promote the Science and Innovation Center and SONPA . Maintains accurate program records, operational data, and reports to support academic, accreditation, and institutional needs. Participates in departmental and University committees, supports the broader mission of the School of Nursing and Physician Assistant Studies, and performs other duties as assigned. Performs other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required Minimum 5 years of relevant work experience. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, planning, team building and problem-solving skills Strong administrative, leadership, written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated ability to take initiative and ownership of projects, prioritize and multi-task. Demonstrated ability to effectively work independently and as part of a team. Work hour flexibility. Proficiency in internet use, computer literacy, and Microsoft applications including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Simulation experience. Experience using EMS -SimiQ software, KB Port software and related camera systems. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Special Instructions Deadline Open Until Filled Date Posted 08/18/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $100,000 - $120,000 Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter (Including Salary Requirement) References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7055": {
      "title": "SEARCH JOBS",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, Literacy Studies Practicum Course Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Literacy Studies Practicum Course Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Literacy Studies Practicum Course Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division School of Education Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description The School of Education is pleased to invite applications for an adjunct faculty position for our Literacy Studies Practicum courses in the Department of Specialized Programs at Hofstra University. Applicants should have knowledge and experience teaching formative reading and writing evaluations, assessment driven instructional planning that includes literature engagements, collaborative learning and multimodal literacy invitations, and strategy assessments. The position also includes the supervision of our interns in their small group literacy support for readers at our Hofstra Reading/Writing Learning Clinic. Qualifications An earned MSED in Literacy Studies with NY State Literacy Specialist Certification is required Initial Certification in ELED or Secondary Education Demonstrated record of working with graduate students in a Literacy Studies Program Successful candidates will have demonstrated a commitment to promoting equity, diversity, and inclusive in an educational environment, and assessment driven instructional planning that includes literature engagements, collaborative learning and multimodal literacy invitations, and strategy assessments. Preferred Quals Summary Preferred qualifications include K-12 public school teaching, and literacy support. Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Teaching statement including evidence of effectiveness as an educator and approach to creating an inclusive learning environment Email address and phone number of three professional references All applications received by  January 15, 2026, will receive full consideration. Inquiries should be directed to Theresa McGinnis /Theresa.a.mcginnis@hofstra.edu Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 01/09/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,458-$1,839 per credit hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Cover Letter Evidence of Effectiveness as an Educator Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
