    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/6172": {
      "title": "SEARCH JOBS",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, Podcasting Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Podcasting Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Podcasting Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division School of Communication Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description The Lawrence Herbert School of Communication at Hofstra University is pleased to invite applications for an Adjunct Assistant/Associate Professor in the area of Podcasting in the Department of Radio, Television, Film ( RTVF ). Candidate should be able to teach the fundamental practices of video podcasting with a focus on the creation and production of chat-style audio programs. In addition, the candidate should have a body of creative work in at least one of these writing practices. The preferred candidate will: Be able to guide students through the full life cycle of a chat show – from concept and development to production and promotion – with a focus on industry best practices. Have a strong command of the technology required to record and edit audio and video podcasts. Have a proven track record of producing and/or hosting chat-style shows Qualifications Proven track record producing or hosting chat-style video podcasts Familiarity with narrative audio and storytelling structures Preferred Quals Summary Teaching experience at the college level Industry connections across sports, music, or entertainment podcasting Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Teaching statement indicating evidence of effectiveness as an educator, including how you will contribute within the department, in your teaching, mentorship, and scholarship. Email address and phone number of three professional references Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 07/01/2025 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,585-$1,711 per credit hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Service Statement Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7698": {
      "title": "SEARCH JOBS",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Senior Executive Secretary, Grade D Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Senior Executive Secretary, Grade D Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra Hofstra University is nationally ranked and recognized as Long Island’s largest private university located in Hempstead, N.Y. When you work at Hofstra, you join a team of talented professionals committed to preparing students for the challenges of tomorrow, in an environment that cultivates learning through the free and open exchange of ideas for the betterment of humankind. The work we do at Hofstra supports the education and well-being of our students, and the workforce of the future. While working towards this mission, employees can take advantage of many enriching experiences on campus. Whether it’s a lunchtime lecture, a Division I NCAA athletics game, a musical concert, a theatre performance, or a visit to one of our two accredited museums, there is always something exciting to do at Hofstra. Enjoy the ease of going to the fitness center, taking a swim, or grabbing a bite to eat without having to leave our beautiful campus! Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Senior Executive Secretary, Grade D Position Number 898561 Position Category Staff School/Division School of Law Department Full-Time or Part-Time Full-Time Description Reporting to the Director of Administrative Operations, the position performs clerical tasks for faculty on an executive secretary level. The position also performs clerical tasks for the law school’s Communications department under the supervision of the Associate Dean for Communications and Marketing. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provides support by preparing correspondence, reports, course materials, outlines, and examination packets. Assists with class evaluations and Canvas-related tasks, including posting announcements and supplemental materials. Supports faculty by screening calls, assisting visitors, serving as a liaison with students, maintaining calendars, and scheduling appointments. Coordinates travel and conference arrangements and processes related expense reimbursements and check requests. Provides backup coverage for other assistants as needed. Supports the Communications Department by creating and maintaining mailing lists for marketing conferences, events, and lectures, including lists of deans, academic deans, and law school faculty. Prepares and tracks Communications Department expense documentation related to advertising and printing. Maintains physical and digital filing systems for archived publications. Updates dates, names, and other information in the website’s content management system. Performs other related duties requiring a similar level of skill and responsibility. Hours: Monday through Friday 9am to 5pm. Subject to bumping Qualifications Minimum of three years clerical experience. Detailed oriented, demonstrated ability to prioritize and manage multiple tasks effectively. Ability to exercise discretion and good judgment. Professional telephone manner, communication, and interpersonal skills Strong word processing skills and proficiency with Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook. Overtime required during peak periods. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education, preferably within a law school or comparable academic environment. Experience with Canvas or other learning management system. Special Instructions Deadline Open Until Filled Date Posted 09/02/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $42,997.00 Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter (Including Salary Requirement) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7556": {
      "title": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Assistant Field Hockey Coach",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Assistant Field Hockey Coach Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Field Hockey Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra Hofstra University is nationally ranked and recognized as Long Island’s largest private university located in Hempstead, N.Y. When you work at Hofstra, you join a team of talented professionals committed to preparing students for the challenges of tomorrow, in an environment that cultivates learning through the free and open exchange of ideas for the betterment of humankind. The work we do at Hofstra supports the education and well-being of our students, and the workforce of the future. While working towards this mission, employees can take advantage of many enriching experiences on campus. Whether it’s a lunchtime lecture, a Division I NCAA athletics game, a musical concert, a theatre performance, or a visit to one of our two accredited museums, there is always something exciting to do at Hofstra. Enjoy the ease of going to the fitness center, taking a swim, or grabbing a bite to eat without having to leave our beautiful campus! Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Assistant Field Hockey Coach Position Number 899240 Position Category Administration School/Division Women's Field Hockey (division) Department Full-Time or Part-Time Full-Time Description Reporting to the Head Field Hockey Coach, the Assistant Field Hockey Coach is responsible for assisting the Head Coach to ensure the program’s success as directly related to the skill development and performance of the student athletes, as well as the recruitment, retention, and conduct of the student athletes. All staff members are responsible for the policy, procedures, and guidelines of Hofstra University and the job requirements specific to the particular assignments inherent to field hockey. This position requires working weekends and holidays and attending athletic events as appropriate. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Assists with the planning and coaching of practices, skill instruction, and development. Assists with recruiting and the implementation and maintenance of a recruiting database. Assists with organizing team travel arrangements, and team game day scouting. Closely monitors student-athletes academic needs and performs other related administrative duties. Assists in managing social media interactions/posts of the field hockey program ensuring they are meeting all department standards as well as NCAA rules and regulations. Coordinates and submits NCAA recruiting, countable athletic related activity, and campus visit logs in a timely fashion in accordance with department, University and NCAA rules and regulations. Adheres to and enforces all policies and procedures of Hofstra University, Hofstra Athletic Department, NCAA , and CAA . Performs other related duties as assigned by the Head Coach. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Valid driver’s license. Minimum 1 to 3 years of relevant coaching experience. Strong communication and organizational skills. Experience using SportsCode and performing video analysis. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Division I collegiate playing or coaching experience. Knowledge or previous experiences with organizing and planning team fundraising events, clinics, and alumni engagement events. Special Instructions Please include a resume, cover letter, and contact information for 3 professional references with your application. Deadline 12/15/26 Date Posted 07/02/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $40,000- $41,350 ( Car Stipend $3000 annual) Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter (Including Salary Requirement) References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/5922": {
      "title": "SEARCH JOBS",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Lifeguard Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lifeguard Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra Hofstra University is nationally ranked and recognized as Long Island’s largest private university located in Hempstead, N.Y. When you work at Hofstra, you join a team of talented professionals committed to preparing students for the challenges of tomorrow, in an environment that cultivates learning through the free and open exchange of ideas for the betterment of humankind. The work we do at Hofstra supports the education and well-being of our students, and the workforce of the future. While working towards this mission, employees can take advantage of many enriching experiences on campus. Whether it’s a lunchtime lecture, a Division I NCAA athletics game, a musical concert, a theatre performance, or a visit to one of our two accredited museums, there is always something exciting to do at Hofstra. Enjoy the ease of going to the fitness center, taking a swim, or grabbing a bite to eat without having to leave our beautiful campus! Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Lifeguard Position Number 999973 Position Category Administration School/Division Swim Center-Operational (division) Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description Hofstra University is looking to recruit Lifeguards to ensure the safety of visitors to our aquatic facility. The Lifeguard will explain safety rules to patrons and enforce the policies and procedures of the Hofstra Swim Center. To ensure success you need to assess situations swiftly and make judicious decisions regarding the safety of swimmers. Top candidates are excellent communicators, swift, and safety minded. This is a part time hourly paid position. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Ensure the safety of visitors to our aquatic facility; communicate and enforce safety regulations with guests, including COVID -19 protocols. Enforce the policies and procedures of the Hofstra Swim Center. Inspect swimming pool areas, locker rooms, and restrooms. Maintain pool equipment and monitor and record pool temperatures. Respond to and take appropriate action to resolve concerns and complaints from guests. Enforce no water play equipment. Keep supervisor/manager informed of situations related to pool operation. Must attend and satisfactorily complete all necessary training programs. Qualifications CPR / AED for the Professional Rescuer. Nassau County Department of Health Lifeguard Card. 0-1 years of relevant experience. Preferred Qualifications Special Instructions Deadline Open Until Filled Date Posted 09/18/2023 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $17.00 - $18.50 per hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Resume Certifications Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
