    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7674": {
      "title": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Coordinator, Academic Success, Zucker School of Medicine at Hofstra/Northwell",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Coordinator, Academic Success, Zucker School of Medicine at Hofstra/Northwell Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Coordinator, Academic Success, Zucker School of Medicine at Hofstra/Northwell Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra Hofstra University is nationally ranked and recognized as Long Island’s largest private university located in Hempstead, N.Y. When you work at Hofstra, you join a team of talented professionals committed to preparing students for the challenges of tomorrow, in an environment that cultivates learning through the free and open exchange of ideas for the betterment of humankind. The work we do at Hofstra supports the education and well-being of our students, and the workforce of the future. While working towards this mission, employees can take advantage of many enriching experiences on campus. Whether it’s a lunchtime lecture, a Division I NCAA athletics game, a musical concert, a theatre performance, or a visit to one of our two accredited museums, there is always something exciting to do at Hofstra. Enjoy the ease of going to the fitness center, taking a swim, or grabbing a bite to eat without having to leave our beautiful campus! Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Coordinator, Academic Success, Zucker School of Medicine at Hofstra/Northwell Position Number 896386 Position Category Administration School/Division School of Medicine Department Zucker School of Medicine, Office of Academic Success Full-Time or Part-Time Full-Time Description The Coordinator, Academic Success supports the planning, coordination, and implementation of academic success programs and services for medical students. Reporting to the Director of Academic Success, this position is responsible for coordinating key operational components of the Office of Academic Success, including academic support programming, learning resource administration, peer tutoring, and student communications. The Coordinator exercises independent judgment in organizing multiple priorities, managing confidential information, and collaborating with students, faculty, physicians, administrators, and external vendors to support student success initiatives. A flexible work schedule, including some early mornings and late evenings, may be required to support student services and programming. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Coordinates the day-to-day operations of the Office of Academic Success ( OAS ) and serves as a primary contact for students seeking academic support services. Coordinates individualized and group academic success programming, including Step preparation activities, workshops, materials for OAS owned courses and related programming. Manages the procurement, payment, inventory, and distribution of academic learning resources, including UWorld QBank subscriptions, NBME vouchers, and other educational resources, while maintaining accurate records and monitoring utilization. Coordinates logistical support for USMLE Step 1 and Step 2 CK examination preparation initiatives, including communications, scheduling, resource distribution, and student tracking. Under the direction of the Director, coordinates the operational administration of the Peer Tutoring Program, including tutor recruitment support, scheduling, session tracking, payroll documentation (if applicable), program communications, and maintenance of participation records. Develops and maintains reports and dashboards related to student utilization of academic support services, tutoring participation, learning resources, and program outcomes to support departmental assessment and decision-making. Maintains confidential student records related to academic success interventions for a student body of approximately 450 medical students. Serves as the primary coordinator for routine communications with students regarding academic support services, appointments, educational resources, and office programming. Supports the preparation of materials, reports, and documentation for the Student Advancement Committee and other institutional committees as assigned. Assists with departmental projects, continuous quality improvement initiatives, website updates, event planning, and development of educational materials. Collaborates with faculty, staff, and institutional partners to facilitate academic success initiatives and ensure timely coordination of student support services. Identifies opportunities to improve operational workflows and recommends enhancements to departmental processes and student services. Collaborates with other administrative staff members to provide coverage during absences, balance workload across the team, and support School of Medicine initiatives. Performs other duties and special projects as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Minimum three years of progressively responsible administrative, program coordination, or higher education experience. Demonstrated experience coordinating multiple projects and competing priorities with minimal supervision. Possess customer service orientation with excellent organizational skills, attention to detail and oral and written communication skills. Must be a creative problem solver with an ability to work independently. Demonstrate a high degree of judgment, discretion, and confidentiality. Must be mission-driven, motivated, and a lifelong learner. Extensive computing experience and demonstrate proficiency with Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Outlook. A flexible work schedule, including some early mornings and late evenings, may be required to support extended student services. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in medical education, higher education, or student affairs. Experience coordinating student support programs, tutoring programs, advising initiatives, or academic success services. Experience with educational technologies, learning management systems, or student information systems. Experience with data tracking, assessment, or program evaluation. Special Instructions Deadline Open Until Filled Date Posted 08/27/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $59,000-$63,500 Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter (Including Salary Requirement) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7606": {
      "title": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Senior Assistant Teacher",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Senior Assistant Teacher Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Senior Assistant Teacher Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra Hofstra University is nationally ranked and recognized as Long Island’s largest private university located in Hempstead, N.Y. When you work at Hofstra, you join a team of talented professionals committed to preparing students for the challenges of tomorrow, in an environment that cultivates learning through the free and open exchange of ideas for the betterment of humankind. The work we do at Hofstra supports the education and well-being of our students, and the workforce of the future. While working towards this mission, employees can take advantage of many enriching experiences on campus. Whether it’s a lunchtime lecture, a Division I NCAA athletics game, a musical concert, a theatre performance, or a visit to one of our two accredited museums, there is always something exciting to do at Hofstra. Enjoy the ease of going to the fitness center, taking a swim, or grabbing a bite to eat without having to leave our beautiful campus! Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Senior Assistant Teacher Position Number 898209 Position Category Administration School/Division School of Education Department Full-Time or Part-Time Full-Time Description The Assistant Teacher s upports the lead teacher in carrying out classroom responsibilities. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provides a warm, nurturing classroom environment for children. Provides a welcoming environment for parents and families. Follows the procedure and schedule set forth by the staff in the classroom. Assists in the execution of planned activities and overall classroom management. Carries out the mission set forth by the Diane Lindner-Goldberg Child Care Institute and Hofstra University. Fulfills the role of the classroom teacher in his/her absence. Demonstrates understanding and respect for children, their developmental needs and interests, and their family and culture. Displays commitment of continued professional development. Performs other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Prior experience working with young children in a child care setting. Preferred Qualifications Degree in Early Childhood Education or Elementary Education with an Early Childhood Education component/specialization preferred. Pursuit of a Master’s degree in Early Childhood Education a plus. Experience working in a National Association for the Education of the Young Children ( NAEYC ) accredited childcare center a plus. Demonstrates knowledge of the NAEYC accreditation standards, NAEYC accreditation process, and Teaching Strategies Creative curriculum preferred. Special Instructions For consideration, please send a cover letter with salary requirement and resume to: CCI@hofstra.edu. Please indicate ’’Teacher-job#898209\" in the subject line, along with applying through this site. Deadline Open Until Filled Date Posted 07/17/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $30,000-$31,530 Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter (Including Salary Requirement) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/6786": {
      "title": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Instructor, Paralegal Studies Certificate Program",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Instructor, Paralegal Studies Certificate Program Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor, Paralegal Studies Certificate Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Instructor, Paralegal Studies Certificate Program Position Number 999895 Position Category School/Division School of Law Department Paralegal Studies Certificate Program Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description The Paralegal Studies Certificate Program at Hofstra Law School seeks a qualified instructor to teach courses in Introduction to Law, Civil Litigation, Family Law, Real Estate Law, Business Organizations, Legal Research and Writing, Immigration Law, Contract Law, Bankruptcy Law, Wills, Trusts & Estates, Criminal Law, and Information Technology for Paralegals. This is an in-person teaching position designed for professionals who are passionate about legal education and committed to preparing students for successful paralegal careers. The program serves adult learners completing an intensive six-month, 306-hour certificate program. The schedule is Monday through Thursday, 9:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. Teach assigned courses in accordance with the program’s approved curriculum and learning outcomes. Deliver engaging, student-centered instruction that integrates legal theory with practical application. Utilize technology, including the Canvas Learning Management System, to post materials, manage assignments, and communicate with students. Evaluate student performance and provide timely, constructive feedback. Maintain accurate attendance, grading, and course documentation. Foster a professional, inclusive, and supportive classroom environment. Participate in faculty meetings and collaborate with the Program Director to ensure course consistency and instructional quality. Qualifications Juris Doctor (J.D.) from an accredited law school. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Preferred Quals Summary College or adult education teaching experience. Proficiency in educational technology and learning management systems (preferably Canvas). Practical legal experience in one or more of the following areas: Civil Litigation, Family Law, Real Estate Law, Business Organizations, Legal Research and Writing, Immigration Law, Contract Law, Bankruptcy Law, Wills, Trusts & Estates, Criminal Law, or Information Technology for Paralegals. Special Instructions Applications should be submitted electronically and include the following: A completed application for employment. A cover letter describing teaching experience and areas of legal expertise. A current résumé or curriculum vitae. Contact information for two professional references. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 11/19/2025 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $70 per course hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/7521": {
      "title": "SEARCH JOBS",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Part-Time Per Diem Teacher Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Per Diem Teacher Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra Hofstra University is nationally ranked and recognized as Long Island’s largest private university located in Hempstead, N.Y. When you work at Hofstra, you join a team of talented professionals committed to preparing students for the challenges of tomorrow, in an environment that cultivates learning through the free and open exchange of ideas for the betterment of humankind. The work we do at Hofstra supports the education and well-being of our students, and the workforce of the future. While working towards this mission, employees can take advantage of many enriching experiences on campus. Whether it’s a lunchtime lecture, a Division I NCAA athletics game, a musical concert, a theatre performance, or a visit to one of our two accredited museums, there is always something exciting to do at Hofstra. Enjoy the ease of going to the fitness center, taking a swim, or grabbing a bite to eat without having to leave our beautiful campus! Hofstra University is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a highly qualified and diverse academic community of students, faculty, staff, and administrators respectful of the contributions and dignity of each of its members. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Part-Time Per Diem Teacher Position Number 896363 Position Category Administration School/Division School of Education Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description Reporting to the child care director, the teacher is responsible for providing a warm, nurturing classroom environment for children and a welcoming environment for parents and families. The teacher sets the standard of professionalism within the classroom, directing other team members in the following the curriculum, procedures and schedule set forth by the administration of the center. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Following the procedure and schedule set forth by the staff in the classroom. Assisting in the execution of planned activities and overall classroom management. Carrying out the mission set forth by the Diane Lindner-Goldberg Child Care Institute and Hofstra University. Understanding and respect for children, their developmental needs and interests; respect for a child’s family and culture; and commitment of continued professional development. Qualifications Associate’s Degree in Early Childhood Education ( ECE ) or a Child Development Associate ( CDA ) credential required. Experience working in a child care or early childhood education setting. Understands and respects children and their developmental needs and interests. Ability to be flexible and step into different roles as needed. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in Early Childhood Education or Elementary Education with an Early Childhood Education component/specialization preferred. Experience working in a National Association for the Education of the Young Children ( NAEYC ) Accredited childcare center is a plus. Demonstrates knowledge of the NAEYC Accreditation Standards, NAEYC Accreditation process and Teaching Strategies Creative Curriculum is preferred. Work experience with infants and toddlers is a plus. Special Instructions Deadline Open Until Filled Date Posted 06/10/2026 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $18 per hour Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter (Including Salary Requirement) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hofstra.peopleadmin.com/postings/5999": {
      "title": "SEARCH JOBS",
      "description": "Careers @ Hofstra University | Adjunct Faculty, Spanish Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty, Spanish Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information About Hofstra At Hofstra University, intellectual curiosity is not just aspirational – it is central to how we engage on a daily basis. Hofstra faculty work within a diverse scholarly community committed to student success, intellectual discovery, free inquiry, inclusivity, and collaboration. Enrolling more than 10,000 students, Hofstra offers students an array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs spanning the arts, humanities, sciences, business, engineering, law, health care, communications, and more. Our accomplished faculty collaborate with students to explore interdisciplinary questions and produce innovative research that lays the foundation for future personal and professional success. With a beautiful campus in Hempstead, NY, Hofstra’s location seamlessly merges the tranquility of coastal suburban living with the boundless opportunities of nearby New York City. Hofstra University seeks candidates who will contribute to a supportive climate for students, faculty, and staff. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive community. Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Spanish Position Number 999972 Position Category School/Division Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences-Humanties Department Full-Time or Part-Time Part-Time Description Hofstra College of Liberal Arts and Sciences anticipates some opening throughout the 2024/2025 academic year and invites applications for Adjunct Faculty of Spanish in the Department of Romance Languages and Literatures at Hofstra University. The Department of Romance Languages and Literatures welcomes applicants who can teach languages courses in Spanish from beginning level to intermediate level. Classes will meet face to face either on Mondays and Wednesdays or on Tuesdays and Thursdays. Times can range from early morning to late afternoon. The adjunct faculty member’s responsibilities will include, but are not limited to: Acting as the instructor of record on a contingent, adjunct basis in the Department of Romance Languages and Literatures for courses in Spanish, from elementary to high intermediate. Teach a range of Spanish-language courses, from elementary to high intermediate levels. Qualifications Master’s degree in Spanish or in a related field. Preferred Quals Summary University-level teaching experience preferred. Special Instructions Please upload the following with your application for consideration: Short letter of application Curriculum vitae E-mail address and phone number of three current professional references (Upon appointment, the successful candidate will be required to submit official academic transcripts and three letters of recommendation.) The Department of Romance Languages and Literatures will continue to review applications until the position is filled. Inquiries should be directed to the departmental e-mail account: RLL@Hofstra.edu. Deadline Open until filled Tenure Track No Date Posted 09/26/2024 EEO Statement Hofstra University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to extending equal opportunity in employment to all qualified individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, marital or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary/Salary Range $1,422-$1,794 per credit Additional Information Hofstra University provides the above salary* as a good faith estimate of the starting pay range which considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience and education. In addition to the salary offered, we offer a collegial and inclusive culture, and a benefits program which includes generous paid time off, paid holidays, tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, and a retirement plan with University contributions. *Salary ranges indicated for positions covered under a Collective Bargaining Agreement are in accordance with the CBA. Documents needed to apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resources Center 205 Hofstra University Hempstead, NY 11549 Phone: (516) 463-6859 Email: humanresources@hofstra.edu © Hofstra University. All Rights Reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
